{"availability":"available","full":"SH1FT-W/casora","name":"casora","description":"A calm, room-by-room dashboard for Home Assistant, with its own Studio.","category":"Productivity","language":"JavaScript","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-04T10:26:48Z","updated":"2026-10-09T17:29:52Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://sh1ft-w.github.io/casora/","topics":[],"demo":"https://sh1ft-w.github.io/casora/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T19:34:52.389Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T19:34:52.389Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T19:34:52.389Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T19:34:52.389Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A calm, photo-backed dashboard for Home Assistant that sets itself up.","Shape the rest room by room in a visual studio. No YAML.","Casora recognises robot vacuums, washers and dryers, dishwashers, 3D printers, home batteries, cars, waste collection, calendars and your network, and gives each its own tile and popup. Room photos for 31 room types, by day and by night, are included."],"features":["It already knows your home. Casora reads Home Assistant's device registry, puts every device into its room and groups what belongs together.","Design it, don't code it. Casora Studio lives in the sidebar. Tap anything in the live preview for desktop, tablet and phone and change it right beside it. Press and hold to try the real popup.","One home, three screens. Desktop and wall tablet show each room with its photo. Phones get a layout of their own with your favourites first.","A popup for every device. Lights, climate, energy, locks, blinds, media, cameras, plants, washers and dryers each open a popup of their own.","Ask first, then switch. Any tile can ask before it switches. When you arm the alarm, Casora names open windows, doors and unlocked locks."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/SH1FT-W/casora/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"2767edaf8064ba7e4c45586